---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import headshot from '../assets/headshot.jpg';

const yearsExperience = 12;
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Corey Wininger — IT infrastructure leader with 12+ years running hybrid enterprise environments. Currently between roles and writing about what I've learned."
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Corey Wininger",
    "url": "https://coreymark.com",
    "image": "https://coreymark.com/og-default.png",
    "jobTitle": "IT Infrastructure Leader",
    "description": "IT infrastructure leader writing about IT operations, AI for the enterprise, and hybrid cloud economics.",
    "sameAs": [
      "https://www.linkedin.com/in/coreywininger/",
      "https://github.com/coreywininger"
    ]
  })} />
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent-primary">
        About
      </p>
      <h1 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-5xl">
        Hi, I'm Corey.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary">
        I'm an IT infrastructure leader with {yearsExperience}+ years of
        progressive experience — advancing from Linux Administrator to
        Solutions Architect to Systems Manager — across multi-site,
        hybrid enterprise environments.
      </p>
      <Image
        src={headshot}
        alt="Corey Wininger"
        width={240}
        height={240}
        loading="eager"
        class="rounded-full border border-border-subtle mt-6 mb-8"
      />
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-invert">
      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>
        I run IT operations. That means incident and change discipline,
        hybrid cloud architecture, CI/CD and IaC, vendor and MSP
        management, and the unglamorous work of making sure
        infrastructure supports the business — not the other way around.
      </p>

      <p>My most recent roles:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>IT Operations Manager</strong> — Heritage / Arcwood
          Environmental (June 2024 – January 2025). Governed a $20.5M IT
          budget, 2,500-user environment, 25+ MSP and vendor partners.
          Role concluded following a corporate divestiture.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Systems Manager</strong> — The Heritage Group (April
          2019 – June 2024). Directed 5 senior engineers, led the CI/CD +
          IaC platform build, reduced deployment cadence from quarterly
          to bi-weekly, and provided architectural oversight for Azure
          and AWS workloads.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Earlier roles</strong> — Solutions Architect, Linux
          Administrator, Systems Administrator across HR, plant
          operations, VDI, and large-scale patch compliance programs.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What I'm doing now</h2>
      <p>
        Currently between roles. Targeting Senior IT Manager, IT
        Director, and VP of IT positions — on-site Indianapolis, hybrid,
        or remote. Also exploring an IT services + AI consulting
        practice, and publishing this blog in the meantime.
      </p>

      <p>
        The live version of <a href="/now">what I'm focused on this
        month</a> is on the /now page.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>
        I translate executive strategy into disciplined engineering
        execution, and engineering reality back into something an
        executive can act on. I believe in ITIL where it helps, skip it
        where it doesn't, and think the best IT leaders treat vendor
        management as a skill — not an inbox.
      </p>

      <h2>Certifications & stack</h2>
      <p><strong>Certifications:</strong> ITIL Foundation</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Infrastructure:</strong> Windows Server · Linux (RHEL,
        AIX, Solaris) · Active Directory · Citrix VDI · VMware ·
        Hyper-V · Azure · AWS · GCP
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Automation & IaC:</strong> Terraform · Ansible ·
        PowerShell · Python · Bash · CI/CD pipelines · container
        platforms
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Governance:</strong> ITIL · incident & change management ·
        DR/BCP · vendor & MSP management · budget management · executive
        reporting
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        The fastest way to reach me is the <a href="/contact">contact
        page</a>. LinkedIn and GitHub links are in the footer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
